::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: rule-unknown-kind fixture ]

==[ import-cycles ]

@rule(import-cycles){
  guard: { twrit: cycles }
}

The writ says this tool holds the rule. It does not -- there is no
`cycles` kind. Skipping it would leave the rule named, guarded on paper,
and held by nothing, which is the failure this tool exists to catch,
spelled one level up.
